      "title": "How it works \u00b7 bake first",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Bake a reference bundle\n\n1. Replace example.png with your own reference image and choose its matching VAE.\n2. Choose the model family in Image RefMod Bake. Each bundle belongs to that family and VAE.\n3. Queue once. The file is saved under models/refmods/<family>/example_character.safetensors.\n4. Open the corresponding RefMod Apply example, refresh node definitions (R) if needed, and choose the saved bundle. The picker uses family/example_character, without .safetensors.\n\nOverwrite is off. Enable it only when intentionally replacing an existing bundle. Connect image_2/image_3/image_4 for more references, within the selected family's limit.\n\n## LTX image guides\n\nThis example fixes the source at 512\u00d7512 and uses resolution=0 so the guide stays exactly that size. Use the VAE from ltx-video-2b-v0.9.5.safetensors (128 channels, 32\u00d7 spatial compression), matching the companion Apply checkpoint. The target is 512\u00d7512. If you change dimensions, change both examples together. A guide must divide the target by the same integer on both axes. Bake one reference initially; extra guides consume additional attention and memory."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Bake a reference bundle\n\n1. Replace example.png with your own reference image and choose its matching VAE.\n2. Choose the model family in Image RefMod Bake. Each bundle belongs to that family and VAE.\n3. Queue once. The file is saved under models/refmods/<family>/example_character.safetensors.\n4. Open the corresponding RefMod Apply example, refresh node definitions (R) if needed, and choose the saved bundle. The picker uses family/example_character, without .safetensors.\n\nOverwrite is off. Enable it only when intentionally replacing an existing bundle. Connect image_2/image_3/image_4 for more references, within the selected family's limit.\n\n## LTX image guides\n\nThis example fixes the source at 512\u00d7512 and uses resolution=0 so the guide stays exactly that size. Use the VAE from ltx-video-2b-v0.9.5.safetensors (128 channels, 32\u00d7 spatial compression), matching the companion Apply checkpoint. The target is 512\u00d7512. If you change dimensions, change both examples together. A guide must divide the target by the same integer on both axes. Bake one reference initially; extra guides consume additional attention and memory."
      }
    }
